@startuml PreviewPanda - Politica de concurrencia

title PreviewPanda — Dos pushes seguidos al mismo PR (concurrency group)

actor Desarrollador as Dev
participant "GitHub" as GH
participant "Cola de Actions\n(group: preview-pr-<n>)" as Queue
participant "Run A\n(preview.yml)" as RunA
participant "Run B\n(preview.yml)" as RunB
participant "S3 (state)" as S3

Dev -> GH : push 1 al PR #<n>
GH -> Queue : encola Run A\n(group preview-pr-<n>)
Queue -> RunA : arranca\n(cola vacia)
RunA -> S3 : terraform apply\n(usa el lock del state)

Dev -> GH : push 2, a los pocos segundos
GH -> Queue : encola Run B\n(mismo group)

note over Queue
  cancel-in-progress: false
  Run B NO cancela a Run A:
  espera a que termine.
end note

Queue -> RunB : en espera...
RunA -> S3 : termina el apply,\nlibera el state
RunA --> GH : check "preview" (success)

Queue -> RunB : recien ahora arranca
RunB -> S3 : terraform apply\n(con el commit 2)
RunB --> GH : check "preview" (success)

note over S3
  El state nunca lo tocan
  dos applies a la vez:
  la cola los serializa,
  no corren en paralelo.
end note

@enduml
